TUNDE AI
AI Receptionist & Appointment Booking Platform for Auto Repair Shops
Product Development Requirements — Version 1.0

1. Product Overview
Tunde AI is an AI-powered receptionist platform specifically designed for automotive repair shops, collision centers, tire shops, and other automotive service businesses.

The purpose of Tunde AI is simple: Help automotive businesses stop losing potential customers because of missed phone calls.

When a customer calls an auto repair shop and nobody answers, there is a significant risk that the customer will hang up and call another shop.

We want to solve this problem by creating an intelligent, human-sounding AI receptionist that can automatically answer incoming calls, communicate naturally with customers, collect vehicle and service information, schedule appointments, and notify the business owner.

Our marketing will highlight that missed calls can potentially represent tens of thousands of dollars in lost monthly revenue for high-volume shops. The often-mentioned $50,000 figure is a potential scenario, not a verified industry average.

The ultimate goal is to build a platform that acts like a real, professional service advisor working 24/7.

The software must be reliable, easy to use, highly customizable, and scalable to thousands of automotive businesses.

2. AI Phone Answering System
This is the most important feature of the entire platform.

The AI receptionist must be capable of answering incoming customer phone calls whenever the shop cannot answer.

Phone connectivity requirements:

Integrate with existing shop landline numbers.

Integrate with business cell phone numbers.

Support traditional business phone systems and VoIP systems.

Allow shops to keep their existing phone numbers whenever technically possible.

Support conditional call forwarding when the shop doesn't answer.

Support forwarding when the line is busy.

Allow owners to activate AI answering outside business hours.

Offer optional 24/7 AI answering.

Support a dedicated Tunde AI phone number when needed.

The system should be designed to work with telecommunications providers such as Twilio or equivalent services.

Important: The AI should not automatically answer every call unless the business owner enables that setting.

Owners must be able to choose when and how the AI answers.

3. Human-Like AI Voice & Conversation
The AI must sound as close to a real human receptionist as possible.

We do not want a robotic voice or a traditional automated phone menu.

The AI must:

Speak naturally, with realistic pacing and intonation.

Understand different accents and speaking styles.

Recognize automotive terminology.

Respond naturally to unexpected questions.

Allow customers to interrupt without losing the conversation.

Handle pauses and conversational changes.

Ask follow-up questions when information is unclear.

Remember information provided earlier during the same call.

Avoid repeating questions unnecessarily.

Maintain a friendly and professional tone.

Minimize response latency so the conversation feels immediate.

For example, if someone calls and says:

"Hey, my 2018 BMW 330i is making a weird grinding noise whenever I brake. Can I bring it in tomorrow?"

The AI should understand that:

The vehicle is a 2018 BMW 330i.

The customer is experiencing a grinding noise when braking.

The customer wants to schedule an appointment.

The requested appointment is for tomorrow.

The AI should then check the shop's actual scheduling availability and offer available appointment times.

The AI must never invent appointment availability or confirm an appointment that has not been successfully booked.

