5. Appointment Scheduling & Calendar Integration
Tunde AI needs a fully functioning appointment scheduling system.

The AI should be capable of booking appointments directly during customer calls.

Requirements:

Real-time appointment availability.

Shop-specific business hours.

Holiday and closure settings.

Configurable appointment durations.

Different appointment categories.

Maximum appointments per time slot.

Different scheduling rules for different shops.

Appointment rescheduling.

Appointment cancellation.

Calendar integration.

Prevention of double bookings.

The AI must understand relative dates.

For example:

Customer: "Can I come in next Friday?"

The AI must know the current date in the shop's local time zone, determine which date the customer means, and check availability for that date.

If the requested time is unavailable, it should suggest alternatives.

Appointment categories could include:

Oil changes

Brake inspections

Check engine light diagnostics

General diagnostics

Tire services

Collision estimates

Air conditioning services

Scheduled maintenance

Other customer concerns

Owners should be able to create their own appointment categories and rules.

The system should support Google Calendar and Microsoft Outlook integration, with automotive shop management integrations added as the platform develops.

For automotive-specific integrations, we should investigate Tekmetric, Shopmonkey, Mitchell 1, and other major platforms.

Where an integration is unavailable, Tunde AI should still provide its own internal scheduling calendar.

