19. Suggested Technology Architecture
I am open to the developer's recommendations, but the system should be designed with scalability and low latency in mind.

Potential components:

Telephony: Twilio or equivalent business phone infrastructure.

AI conversation: A real-time voice AI model or specialized conversational voice platform.

Speech recognition: High-quality streaming speech-to-text with strong automotive terminology recognition.

Voice generation: Realistic low-latency text-to-speech.

Backend: A scalable API and application server.

Database: PostgreSQL or equivalent relational database.

Frontend: A modern responsive web framework such as Next.js.

Authentication: Secure multi-tenant account authentication.

Payments: Stripe subscriptions and usage-based billing.

Email: A transactional email provider.

SMS: A messaging provider supporting customer notifications and consent management.

Calendar: Google Calendar, Microsoft Outlook, and an internal appointment system.

I want the developer to recommend the best architecture based on performance, reliability, cost per call minute, and long-term scalability.

We should avoid building unnecessary infrastructure from scratch when reliable third-party services can provide it.

